hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1390.1","[1390] Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Nafi’, that he heard Abdullah bin Umar say: Whoever sends a loan in advance, only stipulates that it must be repaid. Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 1390 Arabic Hadith:"
"1390.2","[1390] Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Nafi’, that he heard Abdullah bin Umar say: Whoever sends a loan in advance, only stipulates that it must be repaid. Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 1390 Arabic Hadith:"
"1391.1","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi', from Hakim ibn Hizam, that he bought food that Amir al-Mu'minin Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, had ordered for the people. Hakim ibn Hizam then sold the food before he had taken possession of it. This reached Amir al-Mu'minin Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, so he returned it to him and said, \"Do not sell food that you have bought until you have taken possession of it.\""
"1391.2","Malik related to me that it reached him that Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: \"Whoever gives a loan, let him not stipulate anything more than it. Even if it is a handful of fodder, it is usury.\""
"1392.1","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that he asked Salim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Umar about renting out fields. He said"
"1392.2","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that he asked Salim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Umar about renting out fields. He said"
"1393.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf rented land"
"1393.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf rented land"
"1394.1","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to rent out his land for gold and silver. Malik was asked about a man who rented his field for 100 sa of dates or part of its produce of wheat or from other than its produce. He disapproved of that"
"1394.2","Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to rent out his land for gold and silver. Malik was asked about a man who rented his field for 100 sa of dates or part of its produce of wheat or from other than its produce. He disapproved of that"
